1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,512
The Rule 7.5 Zero Program.

2
00:00:03,462 --> 00:00:07,187
Sourcegraph finds, Parasoft decides.

3
00:00:07,187 --> 00:00:16,975
In about three minutes, we take a real C code base from one thousand and ninety five MISRA C 2025 findings to a verified, revertable zero.

4
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:23,712
iso14229 is a real open source diagnostic protocol stack.

5
00:00:23,662 --> 00:00:27,162
About seven and a half thousand lines of C.

6
00:00:27,162 --> 00:00:34,687
A full MISRA C 2025 scan reports one thousand and ninety five findings, and every one of them needs a decision.

7
00:00:34,687 --> 00:00:38,200
Nobody clicks through a thousand rows by hand.

8
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:41,175
The pilot starts with one rule.

9
00:00:41,125 --> 00:00:48,762
MISRA C 2025 Rule 7.5 bans suffixes and minus signs inside INT N C macros.

10
00:00:48,762 --> 00:00:53,062
One Sourcegraph query finds every candidate in the seed module.

11
00:00:53,062 --> 00:00:56,625
Eleven results, in about a tenth of a second.

12
00:00:56,800 --> 00:01:00,612
The fix is a versioned script, not a one off patch.

13
00:01:00,562 --> 00:01:06,812
Two value preserving transforms: strip the suffix, and move the minus sign outside the macro.

14
00:01:06,812 --> 00:01:10,837
Two edge cases are excluded and routed to an expert.

15
00:01:10,837 --> 00:01:14,062
The values are identical before and after.

16
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:18,287
After the fix, the same guard query returns zero.

17
00:01:18,237 --> 00:01:22,175
Even the script's own documentation cannot fool the search.

18
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:26,300
Parasoft C/C++test is the judge.

19
00:01:26,250 --> 00:01:31,737
The seed verification scan reports zero findings left, while the baseline had eight.

20
00:01:31,737 --> 00:01:35,162
Search found the sites; Parasoft decided.

21
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:37,137
Now scale up.

22
00:01:37,087 --> 00:01:40,325
The whole repository, no seed involved.

23
00:01:40,325 --> 00:01:43,375
One thousand and ninety five findings.

24
00:01:43,375 --> 00:01:51,062
The biggest mechanical classes are assert macro artifacts, implicit integer tests, and missing unsigned suffixes.

25
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:54,900
Each fix is one commit on its own stacked branch.

26
00:01:54,850 --> 00:01:59,812
The assert macro rewrite removes one hundred and twenty three findings.

27
00:01:59,812 --> 00:02:02,937
Unsigned typedefs remove sixty eight.

28
00:02:02,937 --> 00:02:06,337
Explicit comparisons remove thirty four.

29
00:02:06,337 --> 00:02:09,930
Reversing any step is one git command.

30
00:02:10,030 --> 00:02:13,055
One verification scan confirms it.

31
00:02:13,005 --> 00:02:17,342
One thousand and ninety five becomes seven hundred and sixty six.

32
00:02:17,342 --> 00:02:24,467
Three hundred and twenty nine findings removed by mechanical rewrites, and five rule classes now sit at zero.

33
00:02:24,630 --> 00:02:26,592
Holding zero.

34
00:02:26,542 --> 00:02:30,480
Sourcegraph detects, and the code host enforces.

35
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:34,592
The same query runs on every pull request in under a second.

36
00:02:34,592 --> 00:02:37,230
Parasoft runs in the pipeline.

37
00:02:37,230 --> 00:02:40,092
Code Monitor watches for regressions.

38
00:02:40,230 --> 00:02:45,430
The Rule 7.5 Zero Program, by Engineering Software Lab.

39
00:02:45,380 --> 00:02:47,330
Thank you for watching.
